<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μί-ασμα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιαίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stain, defilement</i>, esp. by murder or other
			crime, <i>taint of guilt</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				169
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				281
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔστι γῆρας τοῦδε τοῦ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					682
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. φεύγων αἵματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τῶν φυτευσάντων λαβεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1012
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ προσῆκον μίασμα εἰς οἴκους
					εἰσάγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					4.1.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τινὸς ἐπεξέρχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.3.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μ. εἰς αὑτὸν δέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					871b
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1420
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				1017
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμάτων μιάσμασι χρανθεῖσα γαῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					265
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>that which defiles, pollution</i>, of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρας μ. καὶ θεῶν ἐγχωρίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1645
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατροκτόνον μ. καὶ θεῶν
			στύγος</span>, of Clytaemnestra, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				1028
			</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. χώρας ἐλαύνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					97
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς μ. τοῦδ᾽ ἡμὶν ὄντος</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				241
			</span></i>: in Prose more generally, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα μεμιασμένον νοσηροῖσι μιάσμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Flat.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
